# Lockstep session (the dwarf king's door and the ladder behind it, local/batch/b32/a7-king): synth/DKSAVE2-king (synth_saves.py king: the original's battle save of savemid-mine in the mine of Rammelsburg, battlefield 0x0B, moved to level 3, the party in the closed room before the king's riddle door). The battle is taken up (paused: Space), the leader walks north-west into the door's wall alarm: the battle stops, card D4 ($MineT17, three metal heads); the copper head (line 2) opens the door, card E5 ($MineB02, the dwarf king Mimingus); line 1 (brush past him, battle -3): the battle goes on with the door's wall removed and the ladder shown; the leader walks north onto the ladder, U: the leader climbs down to level 5 alone (the party split: the level left shown again); 10 passes and Alt-S (DKSAVE1: the level switch, the leader's floor and place on level 5). Q (the party together) is left out: its long pass (the order menu's reset) puts the original's activation check 61 clocks into the pass, where the tester's clock jumps have no mark (local/batch/b32/a7-king, T5); Space (an input after the last dialog, so that its bwait gets the passes of the original's log). Both games' .SAV and .BSV are compared (bwait:<n> = n battle passes in both games)
